{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":"2026-06-12T11:27:35.349Z","tool_name":"replace","tool_id":"replace__72mqhe9k","parameters":{"file_path":"src/dom/mod.rs","old_string":"    /// Returns the value of attribute `aria-{name}` (e.g. `el.aria(\"label\")` reads `aria-label`).\n    pub fn aria(&self, name: &str) -> Option<&str> {\n        let key = format!(\"aria-{name}\");\n        match self {\n            NodeData::Element { attrs, .. } => attrs\n                .iter()\n                .find(|(k, _)| k == &key)\n                .map(|(_, v)| v.as_str()),\n            _ => None,\n        }\n    }","allow_multiple":false,"instruction":"Add NodeData::tabindex method right after NodeData::aria to expose tabindex parsed as i32 on NodeData.","new_string":"    /// Returns the value of attribute `aria-{name}` (e.g. `el.aria(\"label\")` reads `aria-label`).\n    pub fn aria(&self, name: &str) -> Option<&str> {\n        let key = format!(\"aria-{name}\");\n        match self {\n            NodeData::Element { attrs, .. } => attrs\n                .iter()\n                .find(|(k, _)| k == &key)\n                .map(|(_, v)| v.as_str()),\n            _ => None,\n        }\n    }\n\n    /// Returns the parsed value of the `tabindex` attribute if present.\n    pub fn tabindex(&self) -> Option<i32> {\n        match self {\n            NodeData::Element { attrs, .. } => attrs\n                .iter()\n                .find(|(k, _)| k == \"tabindex\")\n                .and_then(|(_, v)| v.trim().parse::<i32>().ok()),\n            _ => None,\n        }\n    }"}}
